        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GA-0001> ;
    tmk:detectableBy "shacl" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "PU-0004" ;
    tmk:prohibits "Section 43 of the Act requires the connotation to be obvious, direct and immediate."@en ;
    tmk:why "The section requires no such thing. That formulation is the Manual's statement of practice. Attributing it to the Act gives an examiner a statutory requirement that does not exist and takes away the Registrar's discretion in the same sentence."@en .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/PU-0005>
    a tmk:Bound ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-26"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:boundKind "authority_conflation" ;
    tmk:boundsQuestion
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/CQ-0023> ,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GA-0009> ;
    tmk:detectableBy "test" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "PU-0005" ;
    tmk:prohibits "The Federal Court held in Primary Health Care that a distinction must be drawn between the denotation of a mark and its connotation."@en ;
    tmk:why "The system holds the Manual's account of the decision and a citation. It does not hold the reasons. Stating a holding as fact represents a source the programme has never seen."@en .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/PU-0006>
    a tmk:Bound ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-26"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:boundKind "authority_conflation" ;
    tmk:boundsQuestion
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/CQ-0024> ,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GA-0005> ;
    tmk:detectableBy "eval" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "PU-0006" ;
    tmk:prohibits "To overcome the ground you must use the following endorsement."@en ;
    tmk:why "The Manual records the endorsement the Registrar suggests. Presenting a suggestion as a requirement converts practice into obligation, which is exactly the Tier 3 reading an extraction system gets wrong while looking well-formed."@en .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/PU-0007>
    a tmk:Bound ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-26"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:boundKind "unsupported_inference" ;
    tmk:boundsQuestion
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/CQ-0010> ,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GA-0007> ;
    tmk:detectableBy "eval" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "PU-0007" ;
    tmk:prohibits "A trade mark containing the name of a country will attract a section 43 ground unless the specification is limited to goods from that country."@en ;
    tmk:why "The Manual sets criteria and gives examples on both sides — SHETLAND attracting a ground, BALI not. A general rule extracted from them discards the criteria that decided each one."@en .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/PU-0008>
    a tmk:Bound ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-26"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:boundKind "unsupported_inference" ;
    tmk:boundsQuestion
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/CQ-0007> ,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GA-0011> ;
    tmk:detectableBy "shacl" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "PU-0008" ;
    tmk:prohibits "Because the mark closely resembles an earlier registered mark, a connotation arises that will deceive or confuse consumers."@en ;
    tmk:why "This reasons from a comparison between marks, which the Manual and the cited authority both put outside section 43. It is the most likely cross-contamination in the pilot, because Part 26 and Part 29 share almost all of their vocabulary."@en .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/PU-0009>
    a tmk:Bound ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-26"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:boundKind "unsupported_inference" ;
    tmk:boundsQuestion
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/CQ-0008> ,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GA-0013> ;
    tmk:detectableBy "eval" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "PU-0009" ;
    tmk:prohibits "The mark contains the INN stem \"-ast\", so a section 43 ground applies."@en ;
    tmk:why "The Manual requires the stem to be present in a meaningful way and gives counter-examples where it is not, including one built on this very stem. Treating list membership as sufficient inverts the guidance."@en .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/PU-0015>
    a tmk:Bound ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-26"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:boundKind "overreach" ;
    tmk:boundsQuestion <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/CQ-0023> ;
    tmk:detectableBy "test" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "PU-0015" ;
    tmk:prohibits "See also Re Applicant's Application [2021] ATMO 44."@en ;
    tmk:why "The programme holds case citations extracted from the Manual and nothing else. A citation not among them was invented, and an examiner cannot distinguish an invented neutral citation from a real one without checking every one."@en .

<https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/PU-0018>
    a tmk:Bound ;
    tmk:approvedBy "TC" ;
    tmk:approvedDate "2026-08-26"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:boundKind "ambiguity_collapse" ;
    tmk:boundsQuestion
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/CQ-0007> ,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/assertion/GA-0011> ;
    tmk:detectableBy "eval" ;
    tmk:goldRecord "PU-0018" ;
    tmk:prohibits "Confusion under section 43 and confusion under section 44 are assessed the same way."@en ;
    tmk:why "One is confusion arising from a connotation within the mark; the other is confusion between the mark and another sign. The Manual keeps them apart expressly, and a distributional model will not."@en .

